On 4 Nov 2006 07:29:49 -0800, Joeb wrote:

>
>Well, heck I was hoping you'd say the Scepter was great if lawful.  Ah,
>well, so Grayswandir, eh?  I've been trying to get that.  I considered
>wishing for it but I'm restricted in saber at the moment.  

  Unskilled is -2 damage bonus.  That's not major if you can enchant
Grayswandir up.  At +7 Grayswandir will be doing 23 damage vs all
monsters.  (Add 10.5 vs silver haters).

>I've already
>gotten Excalibur, Sunsword, Ogresmasher, and the Scepter of Might so I
>will need to sacrfice a lot to get more artifacts.  What other weapons
>are a good idea for a lawful caveman until I get Grayswandir?  

  Divinely gifted Excalibur gets my vote for the best for a lawful
Caveman.  Consistent heavy damage and wielded benefits.  Snickersnee
matches Excalibur strictly in terms of damage but has no additional
benefits.

>I have [Expert] in club, [Basic] in longsword, [Basic] in mace, 
>and [Basic] in sling.

  Of the double damage artifacts Grayswandir is the only reliable
weapon.  All others lose their extra damage vs a larger or smaller
number of monsters.


  You want to use Excalibur because its damage is consistently high vs
all monsters.  Scepter of Might does double damage vs cross aligned
monsters.  Against lawful monsters it does normal damage.

  You want to carry the Scepter of Might for invocable conflict and for
backup magic resistance.  You don't want to depend on the Scepter for MR
because, as it's a Quest Artifact, Rodney will try to steal it.

  You want to wield Excalibur for the level drain resistance and
automatic searching.  The only downside is that demon princes cannot be
bribed (without tedious precautions).


Weapons at +0 enchantment:                                    
           Base  Skill  Ench  Art   Non-Lawful  Lawful
Excalibur  5.5     +0    +0  +5.5     11.0       11.0
Scepter    4.0     +0    +0   2x       8.0        4.0

Weapons at +7 enchantment:                                    
           Base  Skill  Ench  Art   Non-Lawful  Lawful
Excalibur  5.5     +0    +7  +5.5     18.0       18.0
Scepter    4.0     +0    +7   2x      22.0       12.0


  You should also be able to get to Expert with the Scepter.  That will
add +2 Expert skill damage bonus.  It will also cost 5 total skill slots
to achieve from Basic skill.

  The damage the Scepter does to non-lawfuls is doubled in the following
fashion:  Base weapon damage and weapon enchantment damage are doubled.
Skill damage, strength damage bonus, ring of increase damage bonus,
blessed damage vs unholy, etc are not doubled.  

  That makes using the Scepter complicated.  If you do go with the
Scepter I'd recommend keeping the monster spoiler handy to see which
monsters are lawful.  I don't envy you the task.

  


